1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,130
Listen to a talk in a history class.

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:08,290
Petra is an ancient city located in present-day Jordan.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:15,260
It was established as early as 312 BC as the capital city of the Nabataean Kingdom.

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:20,277
The Nabataeans were skilled traders and Petra became a major trading hub

5
00:00:20,277 --> 00:00:26,130
because of its strategic location along caravan routes that linked the East and West.

6
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:33,240
Petra's architecture is unique because much of it was carved directly into the rose-red cliffs of the region.

7
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:37,440
The most famous structure in the city is known as the treasury

8
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,020
but it is actually a tomb.

9
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:44,820
The city also featured a complex system to manage water including dams,

10
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:50,020
cisterns, and water channels that allowed it to thrive in the arid region.

11
00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:55,118
These advanced water engineering structures were crucial for the survival of its inhabitants,

12
00:00:55,118 --> 00:00:59,040
given the low amount of moisture that was available naturally.

13
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:02,280
In addition to its architectural and engineering feats

14
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,220
Petra is significant for its cultural exchanges.

15
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:09,480
As a trading center, it facilitated the exchange of goods

16
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:13,050
ideas, and customs between diverse peoples.

17
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:19,644
This blend of cultures is evident in the various architectural styles seen in the city,

18
00:01:19,644 --> 00:01:24,040
which include influences from Greek, Roman, and indigenous Nabataean designs.

19
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:29,180
Next, we will explore how archaeologists rediscovered Petra in the 19th century.
